[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A JSON-only export leaves an empty HTML source tree behind

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-SOURCE-FILES-MKDIR-NOISE
TITLE: A JSON-only export leaves an empty HTML source tree behind
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A JSON-only export still creates the HTML source-file tree, leaving roughly 400
empty directories under output/html/_source_files. They are pure noise in a
JSON run and they are part of the cold-export cost. Cheapest fix: skip the
per-file directory creation when the requested formats do not include html.
<<<
